          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.091,
            0.511,
            0.114
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4.4 Look Before You Leap!"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.125,
            0.529,
            0.24
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Did you know that it takes the Earth 365.2422 days to go around the Sun and not 365 days? For our convenience, we consider 365 days as a year in a calendar. We are talking about Gregorian calendar."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.245,
            0.529,
            0.359
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This means that, after one calendar year or 365 days, the Earth still needs 0.2422 more days to complete one full revolution around the Sun. This doesn’t seem like much. But what happens after 100 such calendar years?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.551,
            0.127,
            0.916,
            0.333
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.551,
                0.127,
                0.916,
                0.333
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_21_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.176,
            0.359,
            0.677,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Using our understanding of decimal multiplication, 0.2422 × 100 = 24.22 days."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.403,
            0.846,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "After 100 calendar years, the Earth will need 24.22 more days to complete its 100th revolution around the Sun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.442,
            0.847,
            0.517
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In your Science classes, you have learnt that we experience seasons because of the Earth’s tilt in axis and its revolution around the Sun. If our calendar does not accurately indicate the position of the Earth around the Sun, our seasons and our annual calendar will not match!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.517,
            0.847,
            0.557
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To correct this problem, the idea of a leap year was introduced. Every fourth year, one additional day is added to the calendar year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.575,
            0.431,
            0.596
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Making an Adjustment"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
